cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ProteoForge, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ProteoForge: Reproducible LFQ Proteomics and Phosphoproteomics Analysis"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-04-27"
url: "https://github.com/shubhamplus/test"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shubhamplus/test"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  ProteoForge is an R package and production Shiny application for end-to-end
  label-free quantitative (LFQ) proteomics and phosphoproteomics analysis.
  It supports DIA-NN, Spectronaut, FragPipe, MaxQuant, Proteome Discoverer,
  and Skyline inputs, and provides a complete reproducible pipeline from
  raw intensities to publication-ready reports including differential
  abundance analysis, functional enrichment, network analysis, and
  phosphosite-level inference.
authors:
  - name: "ProteoForge Contributors"
keywords:
  - proteomics
  - phosphoproteomics
  - mass spectrometry
  - label-free quantification
  - differential abundance
  - bioinformatics
  - R
  - Bioconductor
